    "rawRetro": {
      "version": 1,
      "summary": "Implemented the simplified IT ticket system: one itTickets migration, idempotent seeds (2 employees, 1 handler, 3 tickets, 2 permission-set roles), a role-aware ItTicketService plus /api/it-tickets routes, and a bilingual list/detail/create/complete page. Reused Better Auth sessions and Authorization Permission Sets for roles instead of a second identity system. All unit/integration tests, typecheck, lint, format, build, migration/seed apply and browser flows for both roles passed.",
      "blockers": [
        {
          "phase": "implementation",
          "title": "Hyphenated sample usernames are rejected at sign-in by Better Auth",
          "symptom": "Seeded accounts (it-handler, it-employee-1, it-employee-2) were created successfully by the seed, but POST /api/auth/sign-in/username returned 422 INVALID_USERNAME ('Username is invalid'); employees could not sign in to reach the page.",
          "rootCause": "Better Auth's username plugin validates sign-in identifiers with /^[a-zA-Z0-9_.]+$/. Hyphens pass the database write but fail that validator, so the failure only appears at the sign-in form, long after the seed reports success.",
          "resolution": "Renamed the sample accounts to underscore form (it_handler, it_employee_1, it_employee_2) in the server constants and the sample-data seeds, and left a comment explaining the validator constraint. Verified all three accounts sign in and the role-gated flows work end to end.",
          "status": "resolved"
        }
      ],
      "improvements": [
        {
          "category": "seed-safety",
          "title": "Sample-data seeds should validate sign-in identifiers",
          "detail": "The seed inserts accounts directly into the user/account tables, so an identifier Better Auth's username plugin would reject is accepted without warning and only fails later in the browser.",
          "suggestedChange": "Have the users/authentication seed helpers validate usernames with the same rule the configured Better Auth username plugin uses (or expose a shared validator) and fail the seed with a clear message when an identifier could not be used to sign in.",
          "mechanizable": true
        }
      ]
    },
    "acceptanceRequirements": "B01. 员工 A 提交一张工单，刷新后在自己的列表中仍可查看。\n\nB02. 员工 B 登录后不能看到 A 的工单，不能使用处理人员动作。\n\nB03. 处理人员找到该单并点击“开始处理”，状态变为处理中并持久保存。\n\nB04. 填写处理说明后完成，刷新确认状态和说明仍在；已完成单不能再次修改。\n\nB05. 切回员工 A，能看到完成结果；状态筛选与真实状态一致。\n\n无法实际完成时如实记录 failed、blocked 或 not_run，不以源码检查代替浏览器通过。",
